# The job-boundary growth guard (tests/check-vm-growth.sh) runs every
# tests/*.ps as a Control-D-framed job in one --jobserver process and holds
# both banks of virtual memory to the baseline after each. A workload that
# cannot be a job in such a stream -- one that never reaches its Control-D --
# is named here, with the reason, and left out of the stream. The population
# is otherwise the whole directory; only the exceptions are listed, so a new
# test is held to the baseline the day it lands.
#
#   <workload>  <why it cannot be a job in a stream>

interrupt_test.ps   an infinite loop with no exit: it never reaches its Control-D, so it would stall the stream. Its own harness (run-interrupt-test.sh) breaks the loop with an external interrupt this guard does not send.
